      "writtenOn": "2013-08-05T20:13:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You do not want to use lists or dicts as default arguments, they are mutable.  if you change the reference, it will change the reference for the default values for subsequent calls.\n\nStrings, Ints, NoneType, etc are immutable, and assignment into the variable replaces the reference instead of modifying it.\n\nIn short: be very careful when using mutable arguments as defaults.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAQn//MM0\u003d",
      "revId": "cb6487e6802b7eaa90c088fdab175633cd61e197",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAQn//LtA\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/token/providers/uuid.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-08-05T20:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Example of something that would cause an issue:\n\ndef test(roles\u003d[]):\n   new_role \u003d get_new_role()\n   roles.append(new_role)\n\nThat example above would make the default argument for \"test\" include the new_role.  It\u0027s safer to just ensure only immutable arguments are used unless you _really_ want to change the default argument at runtime.  Default arguments are instantiated exactly one time per method/function (not on each call, it would be inefficient to do so)",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAQn//LuM\u003d",
      "revId": "cb6487e6802b7eaa90c088fdab175633cd61e197",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
